  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "OUTPUT_VISIBILITY",
      "status": "FIXED_STATIC_V2",
      "detail": "Direct std::io::Write to locked stderr with a leading newline is used for each observation; ordinary write failure propagates through Result. Only destructor cleanup output is best effort. No launcher nocapture or argument change is required to expose successful-test observations."
    },
    {
      "id": "COLLECTOR_SCOPE",
      "status": "FIXED_STATIC_WORKFLOW_V2",
      "detail": "An unexecuted draft unconditionally supplied the target to the failed-only stdin collector. The final workflow removes that call. The unchanged fixed wrapper selects true failed targets and separately uses retention-console for allowlisted PASSED/FLAKY targets; this exact Windows unit target is in that allowlist."
    },
    {
      "id": "SAME_OBJECT_RESTORATION",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED",
      "detail": "Only newly created owned TempDir objects are labelled; explicit Medium is set at creation, captured and compared before the desired label. Retained non-inheritable READ_CONTROL|WRITE_OWNER|FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES handles share DELETE but do not request DELETE. Label set/readback/identity checks operate on those same handles. Surviving objects restore the complete original descriptor text; pending deleted objects close the observation handle and must subsequently be unnamed. This does not depend on clearing an absent label with a NULL SACL."
    },
    {
      "id": "REVERT_AND_ERRORS",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED",
      "detail": "Synchronous impersonation RAII reverts before reporting/restoration/readback, and failed RevertToSelf aborts rather than contaminating another test. Every row object finish is attempted before result propagation. Setup, observation output, positive-control or restoration failure invalidates this fixture; there is no skip or fallback-success branch."
    },
    {
      "id": "REAL_OPERATIONS",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED_PENDING_EXECUTION",
      "detail": "Four token subjects times two outside-label classes run fresh-path read, overwrite, create, remove-file and remove-directory operations. Effective thread IL/attributes/mandatory-policy are observed, and AccessCheck of parent 0x40 and child DELETE uses the same retained descriptors including labels. AccessCheck is separately reported and never substitutes for the physical operation results."
    },
    {
      "id": "TOKEN_BOUNDARY",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED_TEST_ONLY",
      "detail": "The public production token constructors and original strict controls remain unchanged. The full-restricting read-capability alternative is private test code; its read SID is excluded from default-DACL GENERIC_ALL. The probe spawns no descendants and says nothing about loader, process, Job or backend qualification."
    },
    {
      "id": "POSITIVE_AND_NEGATIVE_SCOPE",
      "status": "QUALIFICATION_LIMIT",
      "detail": "Probe success requires eight valid rows, expected effective token state, inside legitimate writes/deletes/readback, outside original reads, host outside mutations, and descriptor restoration/deletion checks. It deliberately does not assert outside denial. A PASS is observation validity only; all old strict/matrix tests and B11 remain independent and OPEN."
    },
    {
      "id": "BUILD_REGISTRATION",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED",
      "detail": "token.rs has exactly one added cfg(test) path module. Existing crate registration uses src/**/*.rs; existing Windows unit target has the runner/setup binaries as test data. The independent workflow selects the original native outer unit label and MSVC platform, not a replacement filtered or mock case."
    },
    {
      "id": "WORKFLOW_CONTRACT",
      "status": "STATIC_ACCEPTED_PENDING_EXECUTION",
      "detail": "Final workflow keeps 120-minute job, original target/platform/setup, no test filter/no new retries/no nocapture, complete tee console, source HEAD/tree/leaves/status snapshots and original PIPESTATUS[0] exit. Existing archive upload is always&&!cancelled. It records tee status separately rather than disguising it as Bazel status."
    }
  ],
